.TH AVR\-REPO\-MIRROR\-LOCATIONS 1 "" "avr 0.5.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-repo-mirror-locations \- List available mirror locations and their cluster IDs.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr repo mirror locations
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List available mirror locations and their cluster IDs.
.PP
Use a cluster ID, datacenter ID, or unique name with `mirror create --location`.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr repo mirror locations
    avr repo mirror locations --json cluster_id,name
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    cluster_id, datacenter_id, name
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses the default organization.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror (1),
